;; A DERIVED rule with chained head constructions: the inner arrow feeds
;; the outer, so head-const staging splits it and the follow-up stage is
;; driven by a struct delta with pruned static replays.  Under a sampled
;; save (compression per<100), a kept (seen ...) row can pin the arrow
;; structs in the heap while the (wrap ...) row itself is dropped -- the
;; follow-up's only delta then never fires on replay and wrap would stay
;; lost.  The seeded re-entry tasks (staging-replay fix) must regenerate
;; it: tests/compression/run.sh loops this program.

union (ty (tint) (arrow ty ty))
table (src int)
table (wrap ty)
table (seen ty)

rule (src 1) (src 2) (src 3)
rule (wrap (arrow (arrow (tint) (tint)) (tint))) <-- (src x)
rule (seen t) <-- (wrap t)
